# Mutant 18 — R-ALIAS-5
# Description: alias creation becomes check-then-write: a SELECT returns 409 if the alias exists, and
#   the INSERT gains `ON CONFLICT (code) DO UPDATE SET url = EXCLUDED.url` so it never fails. Sequential
#   behaviour is unchanged (R-ALIAS-3 still 409), but N concurrent creates with the same new alias can
#   all pass the SELECT, all get 201, and the stored url is the last writer's, not the first 201's.
# Why realistic: "check for a friendly error, then upsert so retries are idempotent" is a common
#   pattern that an agent writes to avoid handling the unique-violation error code.
# Trigger: the R-ALIAS-5 test itself (20 simultaneous creates, same alias, distinct urls) -> more than
#   one 201 and/or GET returns a url from a request that got 409.

